  "body": "# Gaoxy 0.12.0\n\nNative H1/H2 storage handlers can explicitly select\n`http_limits: %{request_timeout: :infinity}`. Upload body reads and ordinary\n`Plug.Conn.send_file` responses then outlive the total request deadline while\nretaining finite header, read and write limits, bounded transfer windows,\nadmission budgets, cancellation and shutdown. The default request timeout\nremains 30 seconds. This resolves the storage-transfer policy requested in\n[#13](https://github.com/gsmlg-dev/gaoxy/issues/13).\n\nThis opt-in supports ordinary native/Plug targets, including Endpoint-owned\nPhoenix and ListenerSet, on H1/H2. H3 and Generation targets, including managed\ngateway targets, reject it with `:unsupported_request_timeout`, whether direct\nor wrapped. Trusted application code without I/O can run\nindefinitely under the opt-in and must enforce its own execution/idle policy.\n`stream_timeout` retains its response-only role; `:request` means the configured\nrequest lifetime, which is infinite when explicitly selected on a supported\nlistener. See the [request lifetime guide](../streaming-responses.md).\n\nTwo compatibility fixes accompany the new option:\n\n- HEAD preserves validated application Content-Length metadata while omitting\n  the body. Without a supplied length it infers the representation length from\n  the body. Existing 204/205/304 rules, malformed/duplicate length rejection and\n  GET framing remain unchanged\n  ([#12](https://github.com/gsmlg-dev/gaoxy/issues/12)).\n- Phoenix's exact `{:shutdown, :disconnected}` WebSock stop reason closes with\n  1000 and normal termination. Restart remains 1012, arbitrary stop errors\n  remain 1011, and explicit close codes remain authoritative\n  ([#14](https://github.com/gsmlg-dev/gaoxy/issues/14)).\n\nAll six Hex distributions and the standalone application advance together to\n`0.12.0`. Use the Gaoxy WebSockAdapter distribution under Phoenix's existing\n`:websock_adapter` dependency key with `hex: :gaoxy_websock_adapter` and\n`override: true`. Dependency pins and vendor provenance remain unchanged.\nThis release adds no deployment or specialist pressure/load qualification.\n",
